WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.860
When you work for the SCP Foundation, you
need to be ready for anything.

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:10.200
That’s why, as part of the elite Foundation
training regimen, senior researchers and guards

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:15.030
are always running tests, even against things
that aren’t recorded anomalies under the

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:16.750
auspices of the Foundation.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:22.930
That’s why, today, for a real change of
pace here at SCP Explained, we’re not talking

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:28.300
about the SCP Foundation; we’re talking
about made-up monster stories crowdsourced

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:29.640
over the Internet.

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:34.739
We’re seeing how the Foundation might fare
against iconic Creepypasta monsters and maniacs

00:00:34.739 --> 00:00:42.670
like Herobrine, Jeff the Killer, the Slenderman,
Eyeless Jack, Smile Dog, and many more.

00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:47.610
We’ve even created all new Mobile Task Forces
to take each one down.

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:51.260
So, could any of them best the Foundation’s
best and brightest?

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:53.310
Let’s take a look and find out.

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:58.290
And be sure to tell us which is your favorite
Creepypasta entity down in the comments below.

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:00.239
Let’s get creepy!

00:01:00.239 --> 00:01:05.590
Jeff the Killer First up, we’ve got everyone’s
favorite disfigured, knife-wielding homicidal

00:01:05.590 --> 00:01:06.710
teenager.

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:10.990
Whether it’s his terrifying visage or the
iconic “Go to sleep” catchphrase that’s

00:01:10.990 --> 00:01:14.540
forever carved into your mind,
there are probably a lot of people out there

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:19.530
who have lost nights of sleep worrying that
this pale-faced monster could be crawling

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:21.000
through their window.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:25.800
But we know what you’re probably wondering
- isn’t Jeff just a serial killer?

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:31.320
Why would the SCP Foundation use up its time
chasing down any old regular human murderer?

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:34.570
We’d ask for you to think again.

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:38.869
Jeff has displayed feats that clearly mark
him as anomalous:

00:01:38.869 --> 00:01:45.200
Despite suffering debilitating burns to his
face and body, he still shows superhuman strength,

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:46.780
agility, and durability.

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:53.250
He’s also able to see without eyelids, suggesting
some supernatural element is at play.

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:57.700
Victims have also reported him dodging shotgun
blasts while stalking prey.

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:01.090
So, how would the Foundation catch him?

00:02:01.090 --> 00:02:05.910
Seeing as Jeff’s modus operandi is breaking
into the homes of his victims while they sleep,

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:10.470
the best method would be staking out a neighborhood
where he’s been shown to be active,

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:15.430
keeping close observations on houses, and
even setting up personnel from Mobile Task

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:20.800
Force Sigma-9, “My Name-A Jeff”,
in vacant houses as honey traps.

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:25.440
Jeff is undeniably strong, fast, and tough,
but if attacked

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:30.770
and surrounded by operatives with superior
tactics, he could be subdued without casualties.

00:02:30.770 --> 00:02:36.360
Then, it would just be a matter of transferring
him to a standard high-security humanoid containment

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:37.450
cell.

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:41.310
Speaking of horrifying creatures that come
to you in the dead of night…

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:42.310
The Rake

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:47.680
This supernatural entity has been around for
almost a thousand years, as far as scattered

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:49.040
reports are aware.

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:54.980
It’s also been reported across four continents
and a huge number of locations within those

00:02:54.980 --> 00:03:00.070
continents - though most recently, it’s
been reported in rural New York State and

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:02.810
Idaho in the early 2000s.

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:09.020
The Rake is an inhuman beast most often known
for its large, frightening eyes and its long,

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:10.610
Rake-like claws.

00:03:10.610 --> 00:03:15.860
Not only does the monster feed on human beings,
but it also produces a traumatic level of

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:17.950
fear in its victims.

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:23.820
Thankfully, an entity like this is far more
familiar territory for the SCP Foundation.

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:28.660
Using their state-of-the-art webcrawler software,
they could catalog reported sightings as they

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:33.960
happen and use clusters of these sightings
to triangulate the location of the Rake and

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:37.680
dispatch field agents to perform reconnaissance
missions.

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:42.220
From there, it would just be a matter of waiting
to strike and sending in Mobile Task Force

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:47.730
Zeta-13, “Rake Steppers”, fitted with
Dr. Dan’s SCRAMBLE goggles to prevent them

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:52.820
from being affected by the seemingly cognitohazardous
effects of viewing The Rake.

00:03:52.820 --> 00:03:57.380
When the creature is placed in containment
and kept in a state of perpetual bright light,

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:02.380
it would simply be a matter of applying a
Scranton Reality Anchor to prevent the creature

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:05.610
from somehow phasing out of containment.

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:09.930
Just make sure you avoid its big, starting
eyes in the meantime.

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:14.650
Though that won’t be a problem with the
next Creepypasta monster…

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:16.090
Eyeless Jack

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:22.330
This stealthy creature has its no eyes on
one thing and one thing only: Your kidneys.

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:27.810
And unless you want to die or spend the rest
of your life on a dialysis machine, we recommend

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:29.980
you keep your distance from him.

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:35.440
He’s discrete, devious, and diabolical,
and if you wake up in the middle of the night

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:39.610
to see him staring down at you, it may be
the last time your body is able to filter

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:41.930
toxins out of its blood naturally.

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:47.520
Thankfully, we have a way to make the Foundation
put a stop to his organ-harvesting ways.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:51.730
Sometimes, to catch a Jack, you need to use
a Jack.

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:57.170
There’s no way to catch Eyeless Jack without
delicious, live kidney bait, so we’d recommend

00:04:57.170 --> 00:05:02.370
sending in someone who has kidneys to spare:
Dr. Jack Bright.

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:07.060
Bright could be the perfect bait without losing
his life, luring Eyeless Jack into a decoy

00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:12.580
house while Mobile Task Force Gamma-391, “Hit
The Road, Jack”, prepares to spring their

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:19.530
cunning trap and plunge this unpleasant kidney-muncher
into a humanoid containment cell forever.

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:22.900
But our next Creepypasta entity doesn’t
want your kidneys.

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:24.870
It wants your life.

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:26.230
Smile Dog

00:05:26.230 --> 00:05:31.790
Our next entity seems like a harmless little
jPeg to the untrained eye - a little freaky,

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:34.450
sure, but nothing to lose your mind over.

00:05:34.450 --> 00:05:38.960
But we know that there’s far more to this
grinning husky than meets the eye.

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:44.570
If some reports are to be believed, this image
may even be connected to the devil himself.

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:49.770
If you’re unlucky enough to see this image
in the world, it may already be too late for

00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:50.770
you.

00:05:50.770 --> 00:05:55.880
Those who see it - typically as an email attachment
from a mysterious address - spend the last

00:05:55.880 --> 00:06:02.050
week of their life in a hell of the mind before
eventually succumbing to a bleak and mysterious

00:06:02.050 --> 00:06:03.050
death.

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:05.110
It’s a classic cognitohazardous image.

00:06:05.110 --> 00:06:10.030
And the most frightening part is that it’s
self-propagating, with one of the only ways

00:06:10.030 --> 00:06:15.420
to even mildly alleviate the effects seeming
to be “spreading the word”, by subjecting

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:17.340
another person to this nightmare.

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:22.840
That’s when we bring in Mobile Task Force
Rho-19, “Naughty Dog”, an elite group

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:28.540
of hardened military programmers hand-picked
from the CIA’s cyber warfare unit.

00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:33.420
They use their very particular set of skills
to design webcrawler software that roots out

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:40.000
and takes down Smile Dog images across the
web, and, hopefully, one day, find the origin

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:41.690
of this whole thing.

00:06:41.690 --> 00:06:43.780
The next creature, on the other hand?

00:06:43.780 --> 00:06:47.080
We’ve given up on finding the origin of
that.

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:48.650
The Expressionless

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:53.220
This entity kind of looks like a terrifying
store window mannequin, except rather than

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:59.120
modeling fast fashion, she prefers to swallow
cats whole and murder hospital staff.

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:01.210
Oh, and she also calls herself God.

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:03.570
Isn’t she just so quirky?

00:07:03.570 --> 00:07:08.740
Her primary abilities seem to be extreme strength
and large, sharp teeth that easily rend through

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:10.060
human flesh.

00:07:10.060 --> 00:07:15.870
Thankfully, not anything the SCP Foundation
hasn’t dealt with countless times before.

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:20.690
Seeing as the only recorded incident involving
The Expressionless took place at a hospital

00:07:20.690 --> 00:07:25.000
in Los Angeles, that would be the most sensible
area to stake out.

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:30.169
A detail from the creature’s original encounter
is also telling: It reacted severely to the

00:07:30.169 --> 00:07:34.840
doctor’s attempts to sedate it, implying
that chemical sedation is an effective method

00:07:34.840 --> 00:07:37.160
of incapacitating the beast.

00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:42.870
That’s why every member of Mobile Task Force
Kappa-99, “Ain’t No Dummy”, is a sharpshooter

00:07:42.870 --> 00:07:47.590
with a tranquilizer rifle capable of putting
a hippo to sleep with a single shot.

00:07:47.590 --> 00:07:51.200
She’ll probably feel less like a God in
her containment cell.

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:58.100
But while this monster is Expressionless,
the next has one very notable expression…

00:07:58.100 --> 00:07:59.520
Mr. Widemouth

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:04.570
Compared to some of our other Creepypasta
contenders, Mr. Widemouth may not look like

00:08:04.570 --> 00:08:10.370
much - but that, our dear friends, is exactly
what this nasty little malefactor wants you

00:08:10.370 --> 00:08:11.460
to think.

00:08:11.460 --> 00:08:16.600
He may look like Gizmo’s slightly demented
cousin, but his intentions are even more sinister

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:18.480
than that of your average Gremlin.

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:24.910
If you’re a kid home on a sick day, Mr.
Widemouth might strike up a conversation.

00:08:24.910 --> 00:08:29.419
After gaining your trust, he’ll try to lure
you to his special place beyond the trees

00:08:29.419 --> 00:08:30.850
for some fun.

00:08:30.850 --> 00:08:35.440
But take it from us, all you’ll find out
there is your doom.

00:08:35.440 --> 00:08:39.550
This crafty little creep’s small stature
and manipulative stealth abilities might pose

00:08:39.550 --> 00:08:44.500
somewhat of a challenge for the SCP Foundation,
but that doesn’t mean they can’t get him

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:47.860
with a little intelligence and elbow grease.

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:53.560
Mobile Task Force Alpha-18, “The Smile Smashers”,
will follow reports of children disappearing

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:57.140
from their isolated homes under mysterious
circumstances.

00:08:57.140 --> 00:09:02.339
Then, using an extra-strength butterfly net
straight from the folks at Foundation R and

00:09:02.339 --> 00:09:06.440
D, they can chase down and capture the nasty
little monster.

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:10.110
But that won’t be the case for this next
demonic offering.

00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:15.760
No, this creepypasta legend is the one that
captures you…

00:09:15.760 --> 00:09:17.380
NoEnd House

00:09:17.380 --> 00:09:21.210
In recent years, there’s been a spike in
interest in so-called “extreme” haunted

00:09:21.210 --> 00:09:22.210
houses.

00:09:22.210 --> 00:09:26.900
If you’re not sure what these places are
like, basically picture a CIA black site with

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:32.850
the occasional plastic skeleton - it’s all
waterboarding, stress positions, and car batteries.

00:09:32.850 --> 00:09:37.440
But even those places are nothing compared
to the nightmare of NoEnd House - it’s a

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:43.430
moving, possibly even sentient spatial anomaly
hiding in a haunted house attraction, and

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:48.150
if you find yourself inside, best believe
you’re never going to see the outside ever

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:49.150
again.

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:54.670
Thankfully, Mobile Task Force Delta-35, “McKamey’s
Bane”, are on the case.

00:09:54.670 --> 00:09:59.990
Around Halloween every year, they use webcrawlers
to detect chatter around NoEnd House events,

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:05.520
so they can swoop in and intercept, preventing
hapless thrill-seekers from being devoured

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:11.040
by the house and providing amnestic treatment
for anyone who has too close a call.

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:16.670
Sadly, the Foundation will not be able to
provide refunds for those who already paid.

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:22.300
Speaking of paying, you’ll really pay if
you even up in our next creepypasta location

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:24.180
of doom…

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:25.240
Abandoned By Disney

00:10:25.240 --> 00:10:29.620
Mowgli’s Kingdom, an abandoned tropical
Disney attraction based on the Jungle Book

00:10:29.620 --> 00:10:32.320
Movie, is abandoned for a reason.

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:38.070
It’s a hotbed for anomalous activity, including
freakishly large mutant snakes, reports of

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:45.060
ghostly activity, and most prominent of all,
a terrifying photonegative Mickey Mouse that

00:10:45.060 --> 00:10:49.500
stalks any hapless urban explorers who happen
to find their way onto the site.

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:54.370
Of course, the Walt Disney Corporation keeps
it all hush-hush, and the SCP Foundation is

00:10:54.370 --> 00:10:57.040
happy to give them a hand on that front.

00:10:57.040 --> 00:11:01.550
Even if the frightening photonegative Mickey
was removed from the site, it’s likely that

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:04.870
another may appear and continue haunting the
site.

00:11:04.870 --> 00:11:09.399
And seeing that the site cannot be moved as
a whole, the Foundation’s best bet is to

00:11:09.399 --> 00:11:14.560
form a perimeter around the abandoned Disney
attraction, preventing anything normal from

00:11:14.560 --> 00:11:17.950
getting in and anything abnormal from getting
out.

00:11:17.950 --> 00:11:23.649
Mobile Task Force Omega-17, “Sons of Shere
Khan”, are ever vigilant and maintain a

00:11:23.649 --> 00:11:26.300
strong presence in the surrounding area.

00:11:26.300 --> 00:11:30.800
But you don’t need to go anywhere for this
next anomalous terror.

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:36.450
If you’re a big Nintendo fan, it might be
sitting in your house right now…

00:11:36.450 --> 00:11:37.600
BEN Drowned

00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:42.680
This haunted NES cartridge of The Legend of
Zelda: Majora’s Mask contains the restless

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:46.810
spirit of its last owner, a guy named Ben,
who...

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:48.040
Well, Drowned.

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:53.060
If you slot this creepy little gaming experience
into your Nintendo Entertainment System, you’ll

00:11:53.060 --> 00:11:58.029
soon find that the soul of Ben is communicating
with you directly, telling you about how he

00:11:58.029 --> 00:12:03.890
died and why his consciousness lingers on,
embedded in the code of the game.

00:12:03.890 --> 00:12:08.670
Thankfully, other than the psychological trauma
of experiencing the game, you’re unlikely

00:12:08.670 --> 00:12:11.380
to be actually harmed by playing it.

00:12:11.380 --> 00:12:16.550
However, Mobile Task Force Beta-51, “Gamers
Don’t Have Rights”, are still on the case.

00:12:16.550 --> 00:12:21.980
They try to intercept all cursed copies of
the game and administer amnestics to anyone

00:12:21.980 --> 00:12:24.350
who was unfortunate enough to play it.

00:12:24.350 --> 00:12:29.740
While it’s still undeniably spooky, it does
feel like a relief to finally find a safe-class

00:12:29.740 --> 00:12:31.460
anomaly on this list.

00:12:31.460 --> 00:12:35.980
The same can, sadly, not be said about our
next creature…

00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:37.200
The Goatman

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:42.000
If you’re a fan of camping, then this malicious
mimic is going to be your worst nightmare.

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:47.279
This monster has existed as a fixture of terror
in everything from a number of Native American

00:12:47.279 --> 00:12:51.410
mythologies to iconic 4Chan greentext posts.

00:12:51.410 --> 00:12:54.320
You may be thinking, “What’s so scary
about a goat?”

00:12:54.320 --> 00:12:59.320
But this thing is no goat - aside from the
fact it’s the Greatest Of All Time at getting

00:12:59.320 --> 00:13:02.310
you to crap your cargo shorts in the woods.

00:13:02.310 --> 00:13:07.470
First, you’ll smell blood in the air, and
then feel an odd electrical static, like the

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:11.380
feeling all around you right before a lightning
strike.

00:13:11.380 --> 00:13:14.980
Then you’ll hear strange noises.

00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:20.830
Something not quite like a voice, like an
animal throat straining to form human words.

00:13:20.830 --> 00:13:25.530
That’s when you might notice your group
of friends has one more person than you remembered.

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:31.510
And the one thing worse than noticing that
is not noticing it, because if you don’t,

00:13:31.510 --> 00:13:35.930
you may end up as the shape-shifting Goatman’s
latest victim.

00:13:35.930 --> 00:13:40.980
Mobile Task Force Theta-11, “Got Your Goat”,
are constantly on the hunt for this one, but

00:13:40.980 --> 00:13:45.630
its extreme intelligence and ethereal nature
make it a nightmare to track.

00:13:45.630 --> 00:13:49.200
But forget nightmares to track, it’s time
for…

00:13:49.200 --> 00:13:50.440
Laughing Jack

00:13:50.440 --> 00:13:54.459
This candy-striped clown from hell is a really
nasty customer.

00:13:54.459 --> 00:13:58.870
Definitely do not engage unless you’re got
a Scranton Reality Anchor on hand, and you’ve

00:13:58.870 --> 00:14:03.750
got backup from members of Mobile Task Force
Iota-40, “Put Jack In The Box.”

00:14:03.750 --> 00:14:09.709
As a former imaginary friend gone rogue, Laughing
Jack is a semi-intangible Reality Warper of

00:14:09.709 --> 00:14:11.500
considerable power.

00:14:11.500 --> 00:14:16.680
He targets his victims with sadistic glee,
pulling them into his dark carnival to experience

00:14:16.680 --> 00:14:19.140
all kinds of nasty tortures.

00:14:19.140 --> 00:14:25.010
Laughing Jack shows no remorse, giggling while
committing every evil act you can imagine.

00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:30.660
You’ll probably only find this clown funny
if you’re already a depraved serial killer,

00:14:30.660 --> 00:14:34.810
and his sense of humor is likely to utterly
break your mind unless you’ve been given

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:38.279
amnestic treatment from the SCP Foundation.

00:14:38.279 --> 00:14:44.870
This is an anomaly that would probably get
along swimmingly with SCP-106, the Old Man.

00:14:44.870 --> 00:14:49.269
They could chat over a few drinks one evening
and share notes on how to cause the maximum

00:14:49.269 --> 00:14:51.920
pain to their hapless victims.

00:14:51.920 --> 00:14:58.230
That being said, few people understand maximum
pan more than the next horrifying abomination

00:14:58.230 --> 00:14:59.769
on our roster…

00:14:59.769 --> 00:15:02.959
The Russian Sleep Experiment Test Subjects

00:15:02.959 --> 00:15:07.970
As anyone familiar with the work of the GRU
Division-P will tell you, the Soviets performed

00:15:07.970 --> 00:15:12.060
some pretty horrific occult activities throughout
the 20th Century.

00:15:12.060 --> 00:15:16.399
One of the most disturbing of these was the
infamous Russian Sleep Experiment, wherein

00:15:16.399 --> 00:15:21.970
a group of unfortunate political prisoners
were dosed on a classified anomalous gas that

00:15:21.970 --> 00:15:26.950
robbed them of their ability to sleep - a
chemical compound that the scientists hoped

00:15:26.950 --> 00:15:32.029
might increase the productivity of their workers
and soldiers by eliminating sleep.

00:15:32.029 --> 00:15:38.050
Instead, over several terrifying days, the
chemical and the sleep deprivation that ensued

00:15:38.050 --> 00:15:41.620
caused the subject to instead become demonic
monsters.

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:46.290
While current accounts of the story suggest
that all the subjects were killed, we can’t

00:15:46.290 --> 00:15:52.160
say for sure there weren’t more out there
or that the experiment hasn’t been repeated.

00:15:52.160 --> 00:15:57.779
As such, Mobile Task Force Omicron-8, “Nighty
Night”, is constantly on the lookout for

00:15:57.779 --> 00:16:03.410
freakish, skeletal men wandering through the
woods, never sleeping, outside the dark forests

00:16:03.410 --> 00:16:06.600
where Siberian gulags used to be based.

00:16:06.600 --> 00:16:08.450
Better safe than sorry, right

00:16:08.450 --> 00:16:13.490
Though, of course, you won’t feel safe at
all if you spent your childhood watching scary

00:16:13.490 --> 00:16:14.620
media.

00:16:14.620 --> 00:16:20.420
Like horror movies, or eerie SCP YouTube channels
-like and subscribe, by the way - or scariest

00:16:20.420 --> 00:16:23.650
of all, a strange little puppet show called…

00:16:23.650 --> 00:16:25.519
Candle Cove

00:16:25.519 --> 00:16:27.750
Feel a little chill go down your spine?

00:16:27.750 --> 00:16:31.430
Oh yes, you remember this show, don’t you?

00:16:31.430 --> 00:16:36.440
You loved seeing all those cute little puppets
going on swashbuckling pirate journeys on

00:16:36.440 --> 00:16:39.410
their adorable boat, the Laughing Stock.

00:16:39.410 --> 00:16:41.959
Though there was always that villain, wasn’t
there?

00:16:41.959 --> 00:16:44.019
You think his name was Jawbone.

00:16:44.019 --> 00:16:49.410
But that’s not what you called him: You
called him the Skin Taker, because he always

00:16:49.410 --> 00:16:52.980
had that long cloak made of tanned human skin.

00:16:52.980 --> 00:16:56.210
You also remember that one episode that was
just all the characters screaming.

00:16:56.210 --> 00:16:59.459
I mean, how could you possibly forget?

00:16:59.459 --> 00:17:04.539
And most of all, you remember asking your
mom about it, and her telling you that you

00:17:04.539 --> 00:17:09.789
never actually watched a show called Candle
Cove - You just sat around watching static

00:17:09.789 --> 00:17:11.299
for hours on end.

00:17:11.299 --> 00:17:15.949
Of course, the SCP Foundation keeps close
tabs on everything related to this traumatic

00:17:15.949 --> 00:17:17.190
childhood memory.

00:17:17.190 --> 00:17:18.190
Mobile Task Force Xi-30, “Childhood Ruiners”,
use webcrawlers to detect forum discussions

00:17:18.190 --> 00:17:19.190
of Candle Cove.

00:17:19.190 --> 00:17:21.980
Broadcasts of the show are seemingly impossible
to contain - All the Foundation can really

00:17:21.980 --> 00:17:26.089
do is track down people who have seen it and
provide amnestic treatment.

00:17:26.089 --> 00:17:31.359
Though trust us, there are things that will
make your childhood far worse than just watching

00:17:31.359 --> 00:17:33.010
Candle Cove.

00:17:33.010 --> 00:17:36.779
Like running into this next iconic monster…

00:17:36.779 --> 00:17:38.269
The Slenderman

00:17:38.269 --> 00:17:41.909
This terrifying entity is powerful as he is
iconic.

00:17:41.909 --> 00:17:47.570
A shapeshifting, faceless, tentacled nightmare
in a three-piece suit who likes to hide in

00:17:47.570 --> 00:17:53.190
forests and abandoned buildings, either stealing
children away or influencing their minds until

00:17:53.190 --> 00:17:59.129
they become his “Proxies” - supernatural
servants who do anything their inhuman master

00:17:59.129 --> 00:18:00.720
asks them to.

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:05.960
The Slenderman is one of the most powerful
monsters in all of Creepypasta, so their Foundation

00:18:05.960 --> 00:18:10.950
certainly has their hands full with keeping
his tentacles under wraps.

00:18:10.950 --> 00:18:15.730
All that Mobile Task Force Chi-90, “Marble
Hornets”, can do is track sightings and

00:18:15.730 --> 00:18:21.259
keep children out of the woods when the danger
of potential Slenderman encounters arising.

00:18:21.259 --> 00:18:24.990
Getting him actually contained basically seems
out of the question.

00:18:24.990 --> 00:18:28.289
Phew, after all this, we might need to relax.

00:18:28.289 --> 00:18:31.960
Maybe grabbing a nice, sugar-free soda and
playing a session of Minecraft might make

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:33.009
us feel better.

00:18:33.009 --> 00:18:34.950
We’ll be safe there, right?

00:18:34.950 --> 00:18:38.409
Well, probably, unless we encounter…

00:18:38.409 --> 00:18:39.509
Herobrine

00:18:39.509 --> 00:18:44.840
The SCP Foundation, funnily enough, is actually
no stranger to anomalies trapped in Minecraft

00:18:44.840 --> 00:18:49.470
- they’ve got SCP-4335 - A Welt In The Crucible
- to thank for that.

00:18:49.470 --> 00:18:52.340
But this Minecraft horror story is a little
more...

00:18:52.340 --> 00:18:53.340
personal.

00:18:53.340 --> 00:18:59.650
Herobrine is a mysterious user with the Minecraft
default skin, except with one difference:

00:18:59.650 --> 00:19:01.789
Completely white eyes.

00:19:01.789 --> 00:19:06.320
This mysterious figure invades different Minecraft
servers, acting incredibly strange towards

00:19:06.320 --> 00:19:08.490
the people who created them.

00:19:08.490 --> 00:19:11.059
What makes this more than just some random
troll?

00:19:11.059 --> 00:19:16.379
Well, according to legends, Herobrine is the
manifestation of the dead brother of Minecraft’s

00:19:16.379 --> 00:19:17.549
creator, Notch.

00:19:17.549 --> 00:19:21.750
Naturally, the Foundation doesn’t want people
running into ghosts on Minecraft, so they

00:19:21.750 --> 00:19:28.200
dispatch Mobile Task Force Chi-69, “Blocked
and Reported”, to quarantine any servers

00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:34.119
where Herobrine is sighted, and spread misinformation
that the crafty little entity had never actually

00:19:34.119 --> 00:19:36.179
existed in the first place.

00:19:36.179 --> 00:19:37.899
What is the truth of the situation?

00:19:37.899 --> 00:19:42.340
It’s unclear, and that’s exactly how the
Foundation likes it.

00:19:42.340 --> 00:19:47.059
So there we have it, folks, how the SCP Foundation
would counteract some of the most infamous

00:19:47.059 --> 00:19:49.789
Creepypasta creeps and creatures out there.

00:19:49.789 --> 00:19:50.789
Which was your favorite?

00:19:50.789 --> 00:19:52.110
Did we miss any of your favorites?

00:19:52.110 --> 00:19:55.820
And would you like to see any of these expanded
into a full video in future?

00:19:55.820 --> 00:19:57.940
Let us know down in the comments...

00:19:57.940 --> 00:20:01.979
If you dare.

00:20:01.979 --> 00:20:12.590
Now go check out “SCP Minecraft World Destroyer
SCP-4335 - A Welt In The Crucible” and “SCP

00:20:12.590 --> 00:20:16.159
Edition - Weirdest Things on Amazon - Dr Bright's
Great Idea!”

00:20:16.159 --> 00:20:19.740
for more bizarre, unexpected anomalous crossovers!

